        "slc_69f65bfbbd9570a11bafe5abbffbfb548effcc5511e5eae5e79066af64fa6286"
      ],
      "text": "FLEX (Forward Learning from Experience) is a learning paradigm that shifts learning from modifying model parameters to building and leveraging an evolvable experience library."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_c15962b476c4ab7d6489922eb9008d91f09d78b9b16c8c52b034c9f9c9e6e767",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "evaluation",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "b749fc351f81d834b71edb13bc7bc0e51cfdc15d",
          "git_sha": "a16fe7449f7dbee0f652714ed312d4277586c029",
          "line_end": 40,
          "line_start": 40,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "gensi-thuair/flex",
          "url": "https://github.com/GenSI-THUAIR/FLEX/blob/b749fc351f81d834b71edb13bc7bc0e51cfdc15d/README.md#L40-L40"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_05418779f22fa410319601637dd01aa33a3b315257b82c5f9617de03d1ae016e"
      ],
      "text": "The paper reports experiments on AIME25, USPTO-50k retrosynthesis, and ProteinGym, with improvements such as 40% to 63% on AIME25 and 20% to 30% on USPTO50k."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_f7a93818d2994014d6f7ce9c72bd82fae8befabf766903ae6d1a5cdbb122b792",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "components",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "b749fc351f81d834b71edb13bc7bc0e51cfdc15d",
          "git_sha": "a16fe7449f7dbee0f652714ed312d4277586c029",
          "line_end": 278,
          "line_start": 273,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "gensi-thuair/flex",
          "url": "https://github.com/GenSI-THUAIR/FLEX/blob/b749fc351f81d834b71edb13bc7bc0e51cfdc15d/README.md#L273-L278"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_f13ac45d7e728c76a65a620a9d62dc4d130457c615cc80f75e1a4c899f3e89f1"
      ],
      "text": "Core modules include actor.py (task-solving agent), critic.py (experience extraction), explib.py (library abstraction), updater.py (dedup/acceptance), memory_retriever.py, and rate_limiter.py."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_44911d8e39912ea551937173f3d00c630abb2092254c023a7f40da446ac470f0",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "orchestration",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "b749fc351f81d834b71edb13bc7bc0e51cfdc15d",
          "git_sha": "a16fe7449f7dbee0f652714ed312d4277586c029",
          "line_end": 109,
          "line_start": 106,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "gensi-thuair/flex",
          "url": "https://github.com/GenSI-THUAIR/FLEX/blob/b749fc351f81d834b71edb13bc7bc0e51cfdc15d/README.md#L106-L109"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_865cc6c8b95e7ca4cb7a85ebf95a654025fbfebb69001103187d06faa1de8e3b"
      ],
      "text": "Training via reject_sampling.py runs a multi-round loop: an actor attempts the task, a verifier LLM decides continue/stop, a critic extracts experiences, and an updater writes accepted entries into the experience library JSON."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_b60dc02eded538752cf5f0c4d508cc2d7dd860839337fbd0c5563f5b7111b5d1",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
